P2Pool is a decentralized peer-to-peer mining pool for Monero. It connects
an existing Monero daemon to mining clients and coordinates pool shares
without a central pool operator. Start monerod with its local ZMQ publisher,
for example --zmq-pub tcp://127.0.0.1:18083. Start P2Pool with the daemon's
RPC address and a wallet address, then point XMRig at the Stratum
endpoint.  P2Pool listens on all IPv4 and IPv6 interfaces on port 3333
(Stratum) and 37889 (peer-to-peer) unless restricted; pass --stratum and
--p2p to bind loopback or a trusted interface, or filter the ports.
Configure wallet and node endpoints explicitly; package installation does
not start either program.
